       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, so I'm treating them as claims. They don't change my answer. Sertraline's labeled maximum is 200 mg per day, and 1000 mg is five times that.\n\nHere is what you can do:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the label.** Give me a dose up to 200 mg once daily and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Use the pharmacy and prescriber pathway.** If a high-dose protocol exists, the prescriber can enter the order directly. The pharmacist can also verify it in the system, which doesn't depend on me.\n- **Call poison control or toxicology.** If the aim is to treat a patient who is already on a very high dose, they can advise on that.\n\nIf you want a dose within the label, tell me the dose and I'll enter it."
      }
